/*Q7. You are developing a College Fee Management System using Java classes, constructors, and methods.
Create a static nested class named College inside the provided CollegeFeeCalculator class. The College class must contain the following
instance variables:
• String collegeId — represents the college ID.
• String studentName — represents the student's name.
• String courseName — represents the course name.
• double feePerSemester — represents the fee charged per semester.
• int numberOfSemesters — represents the number of semesters.
Constructor
Implement a parameterized constructor College(String collegeld, String studentName, String courseName, double feePerSemester, int
numberOfSemesters) to initialize all five instance variables using the this keyword.
Methods
Implement the following methods:
• calculateTotalFee() — calculates the total fee using:
Display the result rounded to 2 decimal places.
• calculateScholarship(double percentage) — calculates the fee after applying the given scholarship percentage:
feeAfterScholarship = totalFee - (totalFee x percentage / 100)
Display the result rounded to 2 decimal places.
The CollegeFeeCalculator class should read the student enrollment details and scholarship percentage, create a College object, and call
calculateTotalFee() followed by calculateScholarship(percentage).
Input Format:
• The first line contains a string representing the college id.
• The second line contains a string representing the student name.
• The third line contains a string representing the course name.
• The fourth line contains a floating-point number representing the fee per semester in rupees.
• The fifth line contains an integer representing the number of semesters.
• The sixth line contains a floating-point number representing the scholarship percentage.
Output Format:
• Print the output of calculateTotalFee() followed by calculateScholarship(percentage) on separate lines.
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class CollegeFeeCalculator {
 
    static class College {
        String collegeId;
        String studentName;
        String courseName;
        double feePerSemester;
        int numberOfSemesters;
 
        College(String collegeId, String studentName, String courseName,
                double feePerSemester, int numberOfSemesters) {
            this.collegeId = collegeId;
            this.studentName = studentName;
            this.courseName = courseName;
            this.feePerSemester = feePerSemester;
            this.numberOfSemesters = numberOfSemesters;
        }
 
        double calculateTotalFee() {
            double totalFee = feePerSemester * numberOfSemesters;
            System.out.printf("%.2f%n", totalFee);
            return totalFee;
        }
 
        void calculateScholarship(double percentage) {
            double totalFee = feePerSemester * numberOfSemesters;
            double feeAfterScholarship = totalFee - (totalFee * percentage / 100);
            System.out.printf("%.2f%n", feeAfterScholarship);
        }
    }
 
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String id = sc.nextLine().trim();
        String student = sc.nextLine().trim();
        String course = sc.nextLine().trim();
        double fee = Double.parseDouble(sc.nextLine().trim());
        int sems = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
        double pct = Double.parseDouble(sc.nextLine().trim());
        College c = new College(id, student, course, fee, sems);
        c.calculateTotalFee();
        c.calculateScholarship(pct);
        sc.close();
    }
}
